      "dates_from": "git",
      "submitted_by": "Kiley",
      "notes": "",
      "body": "I built out a full forecast for the PA-07 House race using real voter data. Along the way I checked which towns are easiest/hardest to call, found the town that best mirrors the whole district, and tried three different ways to forecast 2026; a simple trend, a \"beta\" method borrowed from finance, and a regression model. I then tested all three against real 2024 results to see which actually works. Spoiler: they don't fully agree with each other, so the last sheet lays out where they land and why that matters.",
      "files": [
        {
          "name": "PA07_Analysis.xlsx",
